# Daily blog (Stress Free Flow website)

When the user asks for today’s blog / daily blog / a new blog post, follow this rule plus their paste brief.

## Keyword strategy (Google + Apple blend)

Saved Apple list: [`docs/apple-seo-keywords.md`](../../docs/apple-seo-keywords.md) (+ PDF).

- **Lead with Google:** research 1 primary keyword with clear search intent (problem + solution / how-to / comparison). That is the default post driver.
- **Blend Apple terms when useful:** weave sheet phrases (Mental Reset, Overstimulation, Sensory Tool/Overload, Quiet Rest, Chill out, Calm Break, Mood/Mind Reset, Self Regulation, Recalm, Breath Reset, Reset Stress, Therapy Tools) into title, secondary keywords, or H2s **when they fit**—not as a forced checklist.
- **Do not** make every post an Apple-list post. Alternate: sometimes Google-only angle, sometimes Google primary + Apple secondary, sometimes an Apple-strong topic if Google intent still holds.
- Prefer uncovered or lightly covered sheet terms when blending; check `blogs.json` / `/blog` to avoid cannibalizing.
- Best judgment beats coverage quotas.

## App Store download banner (every new post)

Every new `blog/<slug>.html` must include Apple’s Smart App Banner directly after the viewport meta tag:

```html
<meta name="apple-itunes-app" content="app-id=6757947997, app-argument=https://stressfreeflow.com/blog/<slug>.html" />
```

Do not edit existing posts for anything else when adding it.

## Real search phrases only (user correction, Sep 27, 2026)

Only target phrases people actually type into Google. Verify demand first (autocomplete, People Also Ask, related searches) and use the exact popular wording—e.g. “brown noise vs white noise”, not invented niche versions like “…for sensory regulation”. Audience/benefit goes in the title and H2s, not the primary keyword. If real people don’t search it, pick another phrase or topic. Never invent keywords; treat the user’s topic examples as direction and verify each phrase.

**Required check before writing (every post):** run Google autocomplete (full network) on the primary phrase and 2–3 variations:
`curl -s "https://suggestqueries.google.com/complete/search?client=firefox&hl=en&gl=us&q=<url-encoded phrase>"`
An empty suggestion list means too few searches: reword or pick another topic. Also make sure the searcher's intent fits the app (e.g. "free apps for autism" mostly means communication/AAC apps, so target "calming apps for autism" instead). Put the autocomplete results in the report.

## Audience and click strategy (from Sep 27, 2026)

- New posts target plain-language searches from parents, caregivers, teachers, therapists, and people with sleep trouble or anxiety. Title = exact search phrase + number or clear promise; avoid ending titles in “on iPhone”. Title, H1, meta, quick answer, H2s, and FAQ all match the same phrase. The app is one helpful step, not the topic.
- Prefer higher-demand phrases (e.g. what to do during sensory overload; calming activities for an autistic child; best sounds for sensory overload; sensory reset activities for adults). Verify each with autocomplete first.

